    <h2>9. "But What If AI Makes a Mistake?"</h2>

    <p><strong>Good. You should ask that.</strong></p>

    <p>This isn't autopilot. It's co-pilot.</p>

    <p>AI extracts the data. A human reviews it before clicking "create." AI drafts the email. A human approves it before it sends. AI answers the client question. A human set the rules for what it's allowed to say.</p>

    <p><strong>You control the safety level.</strong> Routine confirmations? Send automatically. Anything involving money? Require approval. You set the line. AI stays behind it.</p>

    <p>AI is not here to replace your people. It's here to free them from the mundane, menial, but critical tasks that eat their day alive. Your people are expensive and talented. Stop wasting them on data entry.</p>

